1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,256
Coca-Cola tested its new formula on

2
00:00:02,266 --> 00:00:04,009
about two hundred thousand people.

3
00:00:04,019 --> 00:00:04,865
They loved it.

4
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:07,001
Seventy-nine days later, it was gone.

5
00:00:07,169 --> 00:00:08,216
1985.

6
00:00:08,226 --> 00:00:09,899
Pepsi is beating Coke in blind taste

7
00:00:09,909 --> 00:00:10,477
tests.

8
00:00:10,581 --> 00:00:12,417
So Coke changes its ninety-nine-year-old

9
00:00:12,427 --> 00:00:12,997
recipe.

10
00:00:13,007 --> 00:00:13,462
Sweeter.

11
00:00:13,472 --> 00:00:14,121
Smoother.

12
00:00:14,228 --> 00:00:15,925
In blind tests, it beats old Coke.

13
00:00:15,935 --> 00:00:16,793
And Pepsi.

14
00:00:16,959 --> 00:00:17,936
New Coke launches.

15
00:00:17,946 --> 00:00:18,874
And America...

16
00:00:18,944 --> 00:00:19,617
loses it.

17
00:00:19,717 --> 00:00:21,425
Fifteen hundred angry calls a day.

18
00:00:21,435 --> 00:00:23,350
One letter was addressed to Chief Dodo.

19
00:00:23,519 --> 00:00:25,262
Coke hired a psychiatrist to listen

20
00:00:25,272 --> 00:00:25,459
in.

21
00:00:25,469 --> 00:00:27,152
Callers sounded like they were grieving.

22
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:29,125
So how did two hundred thousand tests

23
00:00:29,135 --> 00:00:30,121
get it so wrong?

24
00:00:30,334 --> 00:00:31,102
They were sips.

25
00:00:31,112 --> 00:00:33,261
And in a single sip, the sweeter drink

26
00:00:33,271 --> 00:00:34,431
tends to win.

27
00:00:34,505 --> 00:00:35,668
But nobody drinks a sip.

28
00:00:35,678 --> 00:00:37,070
You drink the whole can.

29
00:00:37,286 --> 00:00:38,994
The original came back as Coca-Cola

30
00:00:39,004 --> 00:00:40,747
Classic, and was soon beating Pepsi

31
00:00:40,757 --> 00:00:41,337
again.

32
00:00:41,555 --> 00:00:42,741
Was it all a plan?

33
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:44,471
Coke's president said: we're not that

34
00:00:44,481 --> 00:00:44,991
dumb...

35
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:46,478
and we're not that smart.

